    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0578" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg482"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. Allen.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 111, of the 3d ultimo, reporting that the Korean Government has
                    allotted 900,000 square meters on Deer Island, in Fusan Harbor, for a general
                    foreign settlement.</p>
                <pb facs="0579" n="483" xml:id="pg483"/>
                <p>The Department would be pleased to know what portion, if any, of the allotment
                    has been reserved for Americans.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
